{"name":"Emerging Leaf","hex":"#e1e1cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"emerging","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Becoming prominent; emergent; rising."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of emerge"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emerging"},{"term":"leaf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The usually green and flat organ that represents the most prominent feature of most vegetative plants.","A foliage leaf or any of the many and often considerably different structures it can specialise into."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To produce leaves; put forth foliage.","To divide (a vegetable) into separate leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leaf"}],"entries":[{"title":"Emerging","blocks":[{"text":"Emerging is the title of the only album by the Phil Keaggy Band, released in 1977 on NewSong Records. The album's release was delayed due to a shift in record pressing plant priorities following the death of Elvis Presley. The album was re-released on CD in 2000 as ReEmerging with one original track omitted and four newly recorded songs by the band members."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/db/Phil_KeaggyEmerging1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emerging","wikidata":"Q5370769"},{"title":"Leaf","blocks":[{"text":"A leaf is a principal appendage of the stem of a vascular plant, usually borne laterally above ground and specialized for photosynthesis. Leaves are collectively called foliage, as in \"autumn foliage\", while the leaves, stem, flower, and fruit collectively form the shoot system. In most leaves, the primary photosynthetic tissue is the palisade mesophyll and is located on the upper side of the blade or lamina of the leaf, but in some species, including the mature foliage of Eucalyptus, palisade mesophyll is present on both sides and the leaves are said to be isobilateral. The leaf is an integral part of the stem system, and most leaves are flattened and have distinct upper (adaxial) and lower (abaxial) surfaces that differ in color, hairiness, the number of stomata, the amount and structure of epicuticular wax, and other features. Leaves are mostly green in color due to the presence of a compound called chlorophyll, which is essential for photosynthesis as it absorbs light energy from the Sun. A leaf with lighter-colored or white patches or edges is called a variegated leaf."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Lisc_lipy.jpg/330px-Lisc_lipy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaf","wikidata":"Q33971"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6f/Re-Emerging_%28Phil_Keaggy_Band_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6f/Re-Emerging_%28Phil_Keaggy_Band_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmerging.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Leaf_Varieties_%2815_sp%29.png/500px-Leaf_Varieties_%2815_sp%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Leaf_Varieties_%2815_sp%29.png/1280px-Leaf_Varieties_%2815_sp%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Leaf_Varieties_%2815_sp%29.png/500px-Leaf_Varieties_%2815_sp%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The diversity of leaves, including Bismarckia, Araucaria, Euphorbia, Nymphaea, Colocasia, Hildegardia, Picea, Melocactus, Cycas, Acer, Yucca, Ferocactus, and Ocimum.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeaf_Varieties_(15_sp).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Vein_skeleton_of_a_leaf_%28de-ghosted%29.jpg/500px-Vein_skeleton_of_a_leaf_%28de-ghosted%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Vein_skeleton_of_a_leaf_%28de-ghosted%29.jpg/1280px-Vein_skeleton_of_a_leaf_%28de-ghosted%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Vein_skeleton_of_a_leaf_%28de-ghosted%29.jpg/500px-Vein_skeleton_of_a_leaf_%28de-ghosted%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vein skeleton of a leaf. Veins contain lignin that make them harder to degrade for microorganisms.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVein_skeleton_of_a_leaf_(de-ghosted).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Eucalyptus_foliage_isobilateral_dorsiventral_IMG_0588e.JPG/500px-Eucalyptus_foliage_isobilateral_dorsiventral_IMG_0588e.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Eucalyptus_foliage_isobilateral_dorsiventral_IMG_0588e.JPG/1280px-Eucalyptus_foliage_isobilateral_dorsiventral_IMG_0588e.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Eucalyptus_foliage_isobilateral_dorsiventral_IMG_0588e.JPG/500px-Eucalyptus_foliage_isobilateral_dorsiventral_IMG_0588e.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Near the ground these Eucalyptus saplings have juvenile dorsiventral foliage from the previous year, but this season their newly sprouting foliage is isobilateral, like the mature foliage on the adult tree